{
  "id": "deck-market",
  "name": "The deck market",
  "description": "The deck market, a night market in the shadow between Pylon Forty and its neighbours under the Spine's deck. Two huge pylons pasted with torn flyers; strings of bulbs and red paper lanterns swagged between them; the city's towers and another highway glimpsed through the gap. A row of stalls under patched tarps: a food stall with a wok, a steel pot and skewers on a grill, plastic stools; a glass-repair booth with an eye banner, shelves of lenses and implants and a bright ring lamp; a pirate radio stall with stacked speakers and a glowing receiver; a rail of second-hand coats and rain shells; a little shrine on a crate with candles in red glass. Cracked concrete underfoot, crates and pallets, a cat asleep on the pallets. Loud, cheap, crowded; the easiest place on the Spine to lose a tail.",
